{#
Generated by: Claude Code CLI
Date time: 2026/09/07 19:20 SAST
Version: 0.6
Description:
	Company Performance section body: how this company's own staff are doing, course by course.

	The same report the platform administrator sees, asked of one company. Every figure counts only
	enrolments held by an active member of the company in context, and only courses at least one of
	them is enrolled in appear at all. A company administrator asking how training is going is asking
	about their own people; a platform-wide figure on this screen would be somebody else's answer to
	a question they did not ask, and is not theirs to see.

	Searched, sorted and paged through the shared controls like every other list in the LMS.

	WARNING: a template comment is not a safe place to document syntax. F3 parses its own tags inside
	comments, so a tag written out as a usage example becomes a real tag in the compiled template.
	Keep every comment plain prose: no angle brackets, no comment delimiters, no template tokens and
	no code.
Changelog:
	2026/09/07 19:20 SAST
	- Created so a company administrator can see course performance for their own staff.
#}
<div class="notice">
	<span>ⓘ</span>
	<div>
		Every figure below counts your own staff only. A course appears once at least one of your people is enrolled in it.
	</div>
</div>
{% include '@platform/partials/dataset-search.html.twig' with {ds_name: 'company_performance', ds_label: 'Search courses', ds_value: company_performance_search, ds_action: '/company/performance'} %}
<div id="company_performance-region" data-server-search-target>
	<div id="company_performance-results">
		{% if company_performance_pagination %}
			{% include '@platform/partials/pagination.html.twig' with {pg: company_performance_pagination} %}
		{% endif %}
		{% if company_performance %}
			<div class="table-wrap section">
				<table>
					<thead>
						<tr>
							{% for sh in company_performance_sort_headers %}
								{% include '@platform/partials/sortable-header.html.twig' with {sh: sh, sort_region: company_performance_region, sort_results: company_performance_results} %}
							{% endfor %}
						</tr>
					</thead>
					<tbody>
						{% for row in company_performance %}
							<tr>
								<td title="{{ row.title }}">
									<strong>{{ row.title }}</strong>
								</td>
								<td>
									<span class="badge info">{{ row.status }}</span>
								</td>
								<td>
									{{ row.enrolments }}
								</td>
								<td>
									{{ row.started }}
								</td>
								<td>
									{{ row.completed }}
								</td>
								<td>
									{{ row.completion_rate }}%
								</td>
								<td>
									{{ row.average_result }}%
								</td>
							</tr>
						{% endfor %}
					</tbody>
				</table>
			</div>
			{% include '@platform/partials/pagination.html.twig' with {pg: company_performance_pagination} %}
		{% else %}
			<div class="empty">
				No courses match this search.
			</div>
		{% endif %}
	</div>
</div>
